ion) Regulations vs. cargo-ship regulations; Germany's BSH under the Schiffssicherheitsgesetz with separate passenger/cargo survey regimes). No redundancy confirmed via grep across every blueprint.edn for any other maritime/ferry-related governor keyword. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-H5011) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed. No bespoke capability library exists for ferry operations specifically", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 12, :spec 528, :total 646}", :adr/explicit-scope-note-5011 "the README's own text carries an explicit 'Scope note: passenger water transport, not marine cargo' section naming cloud-itonami-isic-5020 directly -- following the SAME discipline gridtransmissionops/3510 and mobilenetworkops/6120 both established when distinguishing themselves from adjacent verticals", :adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-5011 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword, :maritime-safety-governor, is grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide", :adr/reuse-logistics-shape-closes-family-5011 "the Core Contract and Trust Controls text follows the SAME framing aviationops/5110 and railops/4911 both established, adapted for maritime-specific safety concerns (a sailing dispatch outside a verified passenger-certificate scope, a maintenance release without inspection) -- the third and final reuse of this shape in the transport-mode family this build closes out", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 13, :spec 527, :total 646}", :adr/date "2026-07-09", :adr/thirteenth-spec-authoring-build "THIRTEENTH 'author a new blueprint from :spec tier' build, closes out the transport-mode family ADR-2607102100 opened. '5011' (Sea and coastal passenger water transport) was the last untouched candidate ADR-2607102200's own Consequences section flagged", :db/id -1, :adr/test-status-5011 "kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before comm